{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Sign-In by a Recently Deactivated User",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Sign-In by a Recently Deactivated User\" or \"<ip>|Okta Sign-In by a Recently Deactivated User\"\n\nSuccessful authentication by a user who was deactivated or suspended (user.lifecycle.deactivate / suspend) in the 30 days before the search window and has not been activated, reactivated or unsuspended since. A deactivated account should not be able to sign in; this points to a lifecycle bug, a backdoor, or a session that survived offboarding.\n\nLimitation: a user deactivated, reactivated and deactivated again inside 30 days is treated as reactivated.",
	"GUID": "83c0f1e7-1bc0-431e-884e-c5085c0b677e",
